<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<request-parameters>
<!--
  D192 = "Provisional Natality, 2023 through Last Month" (updated monthly).
  Rebuilt straight from the D192 request form (help/natality-provisional.html),
  every control at its default except:
    B_1  = D192.V20   (Group Results By = Year)
    M_002 = D192.M002 (Births -- the only count measure D192 exposes)
    O_show_totals = false
  IMPORTANT: D192's measure list is Births + "Percent of Total" + a set of
  "Average X" measures ONLY. There is NO general fertility rate / birth rate
  measure in provisional natality, so this era is [year, birth_count] and
  the fertility rate for 2023+ is simply not available from WONDER until CDC
  finalizes those years into the Natality (D66-successor) series. Counts here
  are still worth having: 2023/2024 are Final, self-updating, and more
  authoritative than the Socrata hmz2-vwda month-sum stopgap in natality.js.
  Year is left *All* (D192 only holds 2023+); fetch.js clips to [2023, ...].
  National: O_location=D192.V21 with V_D192.V21 blank (= *All*).
  Response cells: year, Births -> 2-col contract.
  Test: node --env-file=.env fetch.js --type=natality --era=current --years=2023 --out=rows.json --dump
  On a 400: paste the <message> from pipeline/natality_current.raw.xml.
  If it says "Missing parameter O_PR", add
  <parameter><name>O_PR</name><value>false</value></parameter> (D176 needed it).
-->
